  "id": "dowry",
  "term": "dowry",
  "definition": "Dowry is a marriage-related transfer or demand, often involving money, gold, or other assets, within the marriage arrangement. In the supplied source, it is described as a common practice in South Asia and India that is linked to violence against women, including domestic, emotional, and other gender-based violence, especially when payment is demanded, delayed, or judged insufficient.",
